comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-18T12:39:30.335Z",codex-gpt5,"GitHub report evidence 2026-07-18: open Scorecard TokenPermissionsID alerts #17 (auto-release.yml:34), #18 (codeql.yml:17), and #19 (release.yml:15), all high severity on refs/heads/main. These are canonicalized here; no duplicate item created."
  "2026-07-25T23:57:20.362Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: PR #718 now uses read-only top-level permissions in auto-release, Release, and CodeQL while granting each existing write scope only to its consuming job. Pinned actionlint 1.7.12 passed all workflows; Trivy HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerability, secret, and misconfiguration scan passed with zero findings. Final closure remains gated on the next main-branch Scorecard run reporting Token-Permissions 10."
  "2026-09-24T00:09:09.211Z","harness:codex","Live verification on main at abbe424343221168027c36af043264e73e5cc2dc: Scorecard run 35928177082 completed successfully on 2026-09-23. Its JSON check reports Token-Permissions score 10 with reason 'GitHub workflow tokens follow principle of least privilege'. GitHub code-scanning alerts 17, 18, and 19 for the three formerly affected workflows are fixed, not dismissed. The implementation and actionlint/Trivy evidence were already recorded for PR 718 in this item's prior comment; no duplicate work or workflow edit is needed."
  "2026-09-24T00:40:18.064Z","harness:codex","Evidence: CodSpeed OIDC and Nightly issue-alert write grants now live only on consuming jobs. scripts/release/workflow-permissions-gate.mjs scans every workflow in quality:static; live inventory passes, injected workflow-scope contents: write negative control exits 1, and focused gate tests pass (2/2). Scorecard on prior main was Token-Permissions 10; hosted verification of this head remains pending."
  "2026-09-24T00:51:57.857Z","harness:codex","Final local verification: pinned actionlint v1.7.12 passed all GitHub workflows. Trivy HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerability, secret, and misconfiguration scan passed after excluding ignored runtime caches; no findings in the committed project surface. Workflow permissions gate and injected negative control passed their expected verdicts. Typecheck passed."
  "2026-09-24T01:06:05.769Z","harness:codex","Additional gate evidence: the first full static run reached graph composition and exposed one new generic related edge; it was changed to typed discovered_from provenance. The second run reached gate-registry and exposed the undeclared workflow script. The registered workflow-token-permissions gate now passes registry validation; its local-preflight mapping and negative-control fixture are explicit. The remaining static pipeline will be rerun on this state."
  "2026-09-24T01:06:18.922Z","harness:codex","Final registered-gate proof: node scripts/release/gate-registry.mjs passes with 17 owned gates and 24 enforced pipeline mappings; gate-registry and workflow-permissions focused suites pass 11/11; read-only workflow inventory passes; workflow-scope write negative control exits 1."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-24T01:06:05.027Z","harness:codex","Repository gate inventory limits retained release scripts to a minority; a static workflow check belongs in scripts/ and is declared as a blocking local-preflight gate with explicit owner, taxonomy, bypass policy, and negative-control fixture. This preserves the assurance migration ratio."
